<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Compound interest: compounding more than once a year (INNODEMS)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A bank offers \( {@R0@}\% \) per annum compound interest, <strong>compounded {@freqw@}</strong>. {@nm@} deposits Ksh \( {@P0@} \) for \( {@T0@} \) years.</p>
<p>(a) What is the interest rate for each compounding period?</p>
<div>Rate per period \( = \) [[input:ans1]] \( \% \) [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p>(b) How many compounding periods are there in \( {@T0@} \) years?</p>
<div>Number of periods \( = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>
<p>(c) Find the amount at the end of \( {@T0@} \) years, to 2 decimal places.</p>
<div>Amount \( = \) Ksh [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Interest is added \( {@kk@} \) times a year, so both the rate and the time must be adjusted.</p>
<p><strong>(a)</strong> Rate per period \( = \dfrac{ {@R0@}\% }{ {@kk@} } = {@rd(rp)@}\% \).</p>
<p><strong>(b)</strong> Number of periods \( = {@kk@} \times {@T0@} = {@nper@} \).</p>
<p><strong>(c)</strong></p>
\[ A = {@P0@}\left(1 + \frac{ {@rd(rp)@} }{100}\right)^{ {@nper@} } = {@r2(A0)@}. \]
<p>If the interest had been compounded only once a year, the amount would be \( {@r2(w_none)@} \). Compounding more often gives slightly more.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2025010100</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text><![CDATA[nm : rand(["Esther", "Kelvin", "Wanjiru", "Otieno", "Achieng", "Kiprono", "Amina", "Mutua"]);
rd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else float(v);
r2(v) := if integerp(round(100*v)/100) then round(v) else float(round(100*v)/100);
fq : rand([[2, "semi-annually"], [4, "quarterly"], [12, "monthly"]]);
kk : fq[1];
freqw : fq[2];
R0 : if kk = 12 then rand([6, 12]) else rand([6, 8, 10, 12]);
P0 : rand([20000, 50000, 100000, 200000]);
T0 : rand([2, 3, 4, 5]);
rp : R0/kk;
nper : kk*T0;
A0 : P0*(1 + rp/100)^nper;
w_none  : P0*(1 + R0/100)^T0;            /* no adjustment at all */
w_rate  : P0*(1 + rp/100)^T0;            /* adjusted the rate only */
w_per   : P0*(1 + R0/100)^nper;          /* adjusted the periods only */]]></text>
    </questionvariables>
